president trump has continued to make  claims about voter fraud  even saying the election would be stolen  in nevada and it's an issue the i-team  has been reporting on  vanessa murphy is live in the newsroom  tonight here at six o'clock with more  for us vanessa  well denise you can report suspected  voter fraud on the secretary of state's  website here but as the i-team has been  reporting election officials and  leaders in law enforcement have been  telling us  voter fraud is rare but if they receive  credible allegations  they will investigate them now i talked  with  deputy secretary of state of elections  wayne thorley on wednesday and  asked him about voter fraud and leading  up to the election  i talked with both the fbi and the u.s  postal inspection about it here's what  they told the i-team  any evidence of voter fraud in nevada so  far  no evidence whatsoever of  coordinated widespread  voter fraud we have  received a handful of complaints with  some allegations  again they're just allegations at this  point unproven  that we're looking into but no no  evidence  of voter fraud i wouldn't say it's  widespread  i would say that we get reports every  year every election cycle  of potential voter fraud situations and  we investigate them thoroughly  and we hold the people if it's uh if  it's  proven then we hold them accountable  through the u.s attorney's office as of  right now i am unaware of any  incredible reports of any voter fraud  being committed through the mail  on wednesday when i asked thorley to  specify a number about how many  allegations of voter fraud were being  investigated  he said less than 10 i also want to  mention i reached out to the department  of justice  today to find out about any  investigations into voter fraud  here and i did not hear back now we've  also heard concerns about  how to check whether your mail ballot  was received or counted  there are two websites where you can do  that we'll put both of them at  eightnewsnow.com here's a look  at one of them but keep in mind ballots  are still being counted so even though  it was received  there still may be time for it to be  counted again  reporting live vanessa murphy 8 news now
 

